# AZES Comment Header Policy

Every source, configuration, and documentation file that supports comments must start with
the AZES header. Never make a file syntactically invalid just to insert a header.

## Required fields

- `AZES COMPANY`
- `File:` filename (path relative to repo root when helpful)
- `Author:` `AZES_COMPANY`
- `Created:` `YYYY-MM-DD` (set once)
- `Updated:` `YYYY-MM-DD` (update on meaningful edits)
- `Purpose:` short description
- `Layer:` one of `app` | `package` | `tooling` | `docs`

## Conceptual block

```text
╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║ AZES COMPANY
║ File: <filename>
║ Author: AZES_COMPANY
║ Created: <YYYY-MM-DD>
║ Updated: <YYYY-MM-DD>
║ Purpose: <short description>
║ Layer: <app|package|tooling|docs>
╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
```

## Valid syntax by file type

- TypeScript / TSX / JS / JSX / CSS / SCSS: block comment `/* ... */` at top of file.
- Markdown: HTML comment `<!-- ... -->` at top of file.
- YAML / shell / `.env.example`: `#` lines.
- Cursor rules (`.mdc`): header goes **after** the required YAML frontmatter.
- Strict JSON (e.g. `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`): **NO in-file comment**. Document purpose
  in a sibling `*.md` or via an allowed `$schema` / documented `_meta` key only when the schema
  permits it. Prefer sibling docs over inventing non-standard JSON keys.

## Exempt (do not add headers)

- Lockfiles (`pnpm-lock.yaml`, etc.)
- Generated code (`packages/api/generated/**` and other Orval/codegen output)
- Build output (`dist/`, `.next/`, `coverage/`, Turbo caches)
- Binary assets (images, fonts, etc.)
- Machine-generated artifacts listed in the generated-file policy

## Agent rules

- Add the header when creating a new comment-supporting file.
- Update `Updated` when making meaningful edits.
- Never break JSON validity for a header.
- Never hand-edit generated files to add headers.
